<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21016] llite: hybrid IO should not switch BIO to DIO on ZFS OSTs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21016</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Hybrid IO (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13802" title="New i/o path: Buffered i/o as DIO" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13802"&gt;LU-13802&lt;/a&gt;) switches large buffered reads and writes to direct IO on the client. It has been on by default since &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18033" title="Hybrid IO on by default" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18033"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18033&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On ZFS OSTs this is very slow. A direct IO write has to be committed before it completes, and ZFS commits on its transaction group interval, which is seconds, so a switched write sees roughly one DIO per commit interval. Buffered IO has no such wait, so on ZFS hybrid IO turns a fast path into a very slow one. Implementing ZIL support for this path would fix the cause, but that is a long term goal and not planned for 2.18.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For 2.18, hybrid IO should not switch to DIO when the file has a stripe on a ZFS OST. A client sysfs setting, llite.*.hybrid_io_to_zfs (default off), lets a site that knows its ZFS is fast (for example sync=disabled) turn the switch back on.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The client can already tell ZFS from ldiskfs targets: ZFS OSTs report MAX_LFS_FILESIZE as ocd_maxbytes at connect, ldiskfs OSTs report far less. No server change or wire change is needed, so this also covers servers already in the field.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An earlier version of the check was posted under &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13802" title="New i/o path: Buffered i/o as DIO" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13802"&gt;LU-13802&lt;/a&gt; as &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/52822" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/52822&lt;/a&gt;, deep in a series, but it never landed and master has no ZFS check at all today. The new patch is standalone against master.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
