                            <comment id="504285" author="paf0186" created="Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:19:40 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Patch: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69940" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69940&lt;/a&gt; (supersedes the stale ZFS check at &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/52822" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/52822&lt;/a&gt;). Tested on ZFS and ldiskfs: sanity 119j, 119k and the new 119t.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="504288" author="JIRAUSER19584" created="Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:52:12 +0000">&lt;p&gt;One correction to the description:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;cite&gt;For 2.18, hybrid IO should not switch to DIO when the file has a stripe on a ZFS OST. A client sysfs setting, llite.*.hybrid_io_to_zfs (default off), lets a site that knows its ZFS is fast (for example sync=disabled) turn the switch back on.&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ZFS sync=disabled does not help because osd-zfs always calls txg_wait_synced() for sync transactions so sync=disabled is just ignored. Only setting osd_txg_sync_delay_us (default=-1) to 0 or some positive number helps but that's not safe.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
